      "tree_id": "98a180792ceaf9c9d81af683bdda1f1133206a67",
      "message": "comment_once: keep only the oldest copy when two publisher watchers race\n\nOn test issue #48 (2026-10-23, run 39943626205) the Lean checkpoint comment was posted twice,\none second apart: both publisher watchers of the run passed the bot-comment check before either\nposted. After posting, comment_once now reads the comments again and, when another bot comment\nhas the same receipt link or key, deletes its own copy if that copy is the newer one, as the\nacknowledgement pass does. A comment without a link or key is posted as before, with no extra read.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "timestamp": "2026-10-23T11:58:51Z",
